{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Or has tried.</b> All this you ask." "<b>To take to himself a nation from the midst of a nation.</b> That even you were nations like them, as it is written, etc., 'I said to you: each man, the abominations of his eyes — cast away.'" "<b>And in war.</b> For HaShem waged war for them in Egypt." "<b>And in fears.</b> A noun-form of seeing, as in its Targum."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "The phrase כדכתיב ואומר introduces two prooftexts; the first is left unspecified (ואומר without explicit citation), the second quoted from Ezekiel 20:7."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:43.577709998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}